1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://books.google.fi/books?id=vilAMNUXOp0C&pg=PT71&lpg=PT71&dq=barbavara+sparre&source=bl&ots=fB2Gy1Gmay&sig=MdMPYm3t15c8AHS39MAA0-RyrHE&hl=fi&sa=X&ved=0ahUKEwiw88mXhJXRAhWCZCwKHafSDWI4ChDoAQgrMAg#v=onepage&q=ba
2 CONC rbavara%20sparre&f=false:
2 CONT
2 CONT They were married in Ouchy, Switzerland on September 10, 1862. She was very much home at home in Paris, speaking French as fluently as she spoke her own language. She was passionately fond of music. At their first home in Paris, 1
2 CONC 4 Rue Tronchet, Teresita´s drawing room was the meeting place for "many of the Imperial court´s best known personalities", including Massenet, composer of Manon, as Eva Sparre later wrote in her biography of Louis.
2 CONT
2 CONT Teresita returned to her Piedmontese manor, Villa Teresita in Gravellona, near Turin, Spend the summer of 1863 while she awaited the birth of her baby. The little town of Gravellona had been ruled by her family for centuries.
