1 NAME Berndt /Aulin/
2 GIVN Berndt
2 _MARNM Aulin
2 NICK Berendt
2 NICK Bernt
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 11 FEB 1685
2 PLAC Åhus, Kristianstads län, Sverige
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 15 APR 1733
2 PLAC Bösarp, Malmöhus län, Sverige
2 ADDR
1 BURI
2 DATE 12 JUN 1733
1 OCCU Kyrkoherde i Bösarp fsg, Malmöhus län
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Kyrkoherde i Bösarp fsg, Malmöhus län
2 CONT
2 CONT "Bösarp and Simlinge Parishes 12.  BERNT (BERNHARD) AULIN 8 July 1713 Bernt Aulin received the Royal Senate´s letters of appointment to Bösarp and Simlinge. B.A. was born in Åhus 11 February 1685, son of the minister there Olof Au
2 CONC lin and Christina Catharina Rönnow; in 1699 he attended school in Kristianstads, dim. 3 September 1704.  He became a student at the University that same year.  (Blekinge Student Assoc. 24 September)  In 1707 he accepted a situatio
2 CONC n with the vicar Petrus Collin in Everöd, after a year he went back to the Academy.  Later, he was called to assist the vicar Hans Jacobsson in Vittskövle.  Because he did not accompany the Bishop and the Consistory to Osby during
2 CONC  the war he was ordained in Vittskövle on 12 November 1709.  He served there until 8 July 1713, when he was appointed vicar in Bösarp and Simlinge. This appointment was later confirmed by Karl XII, the notice is dated Demotica 10 
2 CONC February 1714.  According to biographical data he was `a faithful servant of God, blessed with sound gifts of the Spirit and he was a good example of piety and duty for his house and his trusted herd of God´s children and his pari
2 CONC sh; a peace loving man, without vanity and deceit, one who wished everyone well, did not slander but turned everything to the best`.  He gave the sermon at the Vicar´s Meeting in 1720.  On 13 July 1724 he was hit by the ill fortun
2 CONC e that the vicarage in Bösarp burned down and he lost all of his possessions.  At that moment, it is said, he came down with `some sort of mental alteration and anxiety´ and never quite healed from that.  Bernt Aulin died in Bösar
2 CONC p on 15 April 1733.  Buried the same year on 12 June (funeral orations were given by his sons Olof, Sven, Johan, Herman, and Jöns and by S.P. Hulteen). Aulin was married in Bösarp 16 June 1713 (according to a speech at the wedding
2 CONC  by his brother Magnus A.) to Gunilla Catharina Munthe, born in Bösarp about 1694, died in Hammarlöv 14 October 1768 at 74 years 11 months and 5 days, her estate was inventoried in Skytts the same year 30 November, the daughter of
2 CONC  B. 10), in her first marriage (married a second time to B.13) . . . Children (7 sons and 7 daughters, 2 sons and 1 daughter died before their father; according to a letter by B.A. written on 15 September 1729, there were 9 childr
2 CONC en:  the following children are known, but the order between them is uncertain; the given order in the mother's estate inventory is Olof, Sven, Herman, Lovisa, Stina, Lena, Greta, Maja, Johanna, and Maria.  This does not agree wit
2 CONC h the age given when the daughters died. Maria (Maja) born in Bösarp about 1713, died in Trelleborg 1778 10/22 "65 years", married after the banns were read in Hammarlöv 1772 1/12 to the former girdle maker later to become a shopk
2 CONC eeper in Trelleborg Christian Landgren.  He died in Trelleborg 1800 1/27, "62 years old in his 2nd marriage (married 1st time there 1765 6/7 to Cecilia Larsdotter, who died there 1771 4/15.  He married a 3rd time there 1778 5/1 to
2 CONC  Maria Catharina Tholin.  She died 1795 7/13).  Olof born around 1714 in B.  Sjm Sk. 1134.  He was an auscultator at the court of appeal. He died in V.Hoby 1782 2/1 "67 years old".  Lovisa Catharina, born in Bösarp around 1715.  S
2 CONC he married the rector in Farhult, the dean Lars Darin.  Christina (Stina) Catharina, born in Bösarp around 1718.  She was married to the rector in Hammarlöv, Petrus Darin. Sven, born in Bösarp 1720 2/14.  Rector in Åhus.  Johan, T
2 CONC he only thing known about him is that he took part in his father's funeral 1733.  Gustaf Herman, born in Bösarp around 1722, population census commissary in Oxie and other places.  He died in Kyrkoköpinge 1782 6/8, "60 years old".
2 CONC  He was buried in Bösarp.  Estate inventory in Skytts district that same year 8/1.  Jons, the only thing known about him is that he took part in his father's funeral.  Johanna Maria.  She had a sponsor in Farhult 1751 1/5 and was 
2 CONC still unmarried 1768 11/30.  Margareta (Greta), born in Bösarp around 1732. Had a sponsor in Farhult 1753 1/18.  She died in Hammarlöv 1800 1/7. "77 years old".  Lena, born i Bösarp about 1733. Died at N. Vrams vicarage,1788 9/21.
2 CONC   "54 years old". Source:  Carlquist, Gunnar "Lunds Stifts Herdaminne" Volume 3, page 218.
2 CONT
2 CONT Länk: [http://www.tjocka.nu/heritage/i50.htm#i6906 Källa]
