1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Coyet_nr_473#TAB_8
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.nad.riksarkivet.se/sbl/Presentation.aspx?id=15632
2 CONT
2 CONT Enlisted in the Army’s fleet in 1788. Commanded a galley in battle in Svensksund (August 24,1789). He was awarded the Knight's Cross of the Order of the Sword of King GustavIII. After the attack on Fredrikshamn (May 05,1790) , whe
2 CONC re he commanded a galley Nordstjerneorden was promoted to lieutenant. During the break  Swedish fleet of Vyborg Bay (June 03,.1790) captured. From 1798 to 1808 he served in the open sea fleet. In 1808, Adjutant of Duke Karl. From 
2 CONC 1815, the commander of the Army’s fleet, then the fleet of Stockholm. Rear-Admiral in 1815, Vice-Admiral in 1823. Developed the concept of protection of the coast of Sweden by the Army’s fleet. In 1843, he retired. For Services to
2 CONC  Sweden in 1849 was awarded the rank of Admiral and in 1853 became a knight of the Swedish Royal Order of the Seraphim.
