1 NOTE {geni:about_me} många dubletter barnen
2 CONT -----
2 CONT Johannes Lechander. Född 1574 i Bitterna (R). Levde i Bitterna (R). Levde i Lekåsa (R). Kyrkoherde i Bitterna (R). Död 1672-02-15 i Bitterna (R). Kyrkoherde. Gift
2 CONT
2 CONT Johannes Lechander. Född omkring 1595 i Bitterna (R).  Död 1672 i Bitterna (R). Kyrkoherde i Bitterna. 
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT '''Jonae Lechander''', Kyrkoherde. Källa Stig Svensson, runeby@telia.com. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Barn:	Sigrid Brinck (born Lechander), Jonas Lechander, Gunnor Knös (born Lechander), Gunnur Boberg Bobergius Knöös (born Lechander), Beata Björck (born Lechander), Elias Lechander, Nils Lechander, Bengt Lechander, Ingrid Lechander
2 CONC , Margarethe Lechander, Elisabeth Lechander, Kerstin Lechander, Magnus Lechander, Erik Lechander, Abraham Lechander.
2 CONT
2 CONT -----------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography from Johan Wilhelm Warholm, "Skara stifts herdaminne (1871), pp. 441-442,
2 CONT https://runeberg.org/skarahe1/0447.html and https://runeberg.org/skarahe1/0448.html
2 CONT "4. BITTERNÅ. Church pastors. . . .
2 CONT 6. Johannes Lechander, son of parish priest Jonas Laur. in Lekåsa, born in Upsalla 1624, became pastor in Bitterna 1633. Died 15 Feb. 1672.
2 CONT Married 1st Gunnur Odhelius, daughter of parish priest Ericus Magni in Dala; 2nd m. Annika Hornius, daughter of dean Arvid H. in Fristad. Children from the first marriage: 
2 CONT Jonas, father's successor. 
2 CONT Erik, royal quartermaster. 
2 CONT Abraham, died abroad. 
2 CONT Sigrid, married 1st And. Brink, 2nd And. Hasselberg, pastors in Österplana. Later married: Elias, died as a student. 
2 CONT Nils, pastor. in Sunnersberg. 
2 CONT Bengt, pattern maker (His son Johannes died as a student in 1728, the last of the Lechanderska family). 
2 CONT Gunnur, married 1st m. commune. Pet, Bobergiiis in Bitterna, 2nd m. hejderidaren Birg. Knös.
2 CONT Beata, married captain Ingem. Björck. . . .
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Residences: birth-1633 Lekåsa (R), 1633-death Bitterna (R).
2 CONT
2 CONT Allan Anderson notes:
2 CONT my mm mm mm mm mf  also my mf mm mm mm mf
2 CONT Johannes Lecharder was the kyrkoherde at Bitterna, and the son of the Kyrkoherde at Lekåsa.
2 CONT He became kyrkoherde at Bitterna, moving there in 1633 from Lekåsa, Skaraborg.
2 CONT
2 CONT Locations: Lekåsa is 16 km. to the east. Bitterna is 4 km SW of Vedum and 7 km SW of Sodra Lundby and 10 km. SW of Larv.
2 CONT From Larv, Bäckebo is 4 km. NW and Vassby almost adjoins to the N.
2 CONT Faleberg is 3 km. S. of Larv. Edsvara is 7 km. NE.
2 CONT Naum (14 km NW of Larv and 9 km. NW of Vedum).
2 CONT Vassby (4 km NW of Larv and 6 km. NE of Vedum).
2 CONT           Backebo
2 CONT
2 CONT S. Lundby                Larv (8 km E Vedum and 5 km E. of Sodra Lundby)
2 CONT Eling           Vedum
2 CONT                                             Faleberg               Ryd
2 CONT
2 CONT    Bitterna (4 km SW of Vedum and 10 km SW of Larv)
2 CONT <---Lekåsa
2 CONT Talanda
2 CONT
2 CONT Interesting family:
2 CONT Johannes Lecharder was the kyrkoherde (vicar) at Bitterna, and he was son of the Kyrkoherde at Lekåsa.
2 CONT His son Nils was Kyrkoherde at Sunnerberg who wed a daughter of a Kyrkoherde.
2 CONT His sister wed Komminister of Skara (R) and Pastor hospitalet and Kållands-Åsaka, Skaraborg).
2 CONT His nephew Sven Larsson was pastor in Tadene, Skaraborg.
2 CONT His granddaughters all wed clergymen.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources:
2 CONT https://gw.geneanet.org/idahl?lang=sv&p=johannes+jonae&n=lechander
2 CONT https://family.brudvik.org/genealogy/getperson.php?personID=I790&tree=brudvik
2 CONT Biography of Johannes and Jonas Lechander, from Assar Blomberg Öster- och Västerbitterna Socknar (1929), pp. 15-16. See attached page image or image at https://www.familysearch.org/en/memories/memory/218602954
2 CONT
2 CONT -----------------------------------
